Revision history for File-Slurp-Remote

0.48	Tue Oct 20 08:58:36 PM EDT 2026
	[ Enhancements ]
	- Allow the remote user name to be given as user@host, as scp does
	- Refuse hosts and user names beginning with '-' so they can't be taken as ssh options
	- user@host is split at the last @, as ssh does, and the user is passed with ssh -l
	- Paths may contain colons: the host ends at the first colon before any slash, as with scp
	[ Bug Fixes ]
	- Paths like ./a:b are now treated as local files
	- Quote the host name in the BROKEN_DNS_WORKAROUND ssh call
	- CanonicalHostnames: add $VERSION, fix POD errors
	- Remove unused temporary directory created on load
	- Document that $File::Slurp::Remote::scp is unused
	[ Packaging ]
	- Declare core, test and minimum perl dependencies; add LICENSE and repository metadata
	[ Testing ]
	- Add t/remote_user.t, which doesn't need ssh access to localhost
	- Add POD and POD coverage author tests, run in CI

0.47	Sat Oct 10 09:36:13 PM EDT 2026
	[ Bug Fixes ]
	- Add missing 'package File::Slurp::Remote' so PAUSE can index the distribution
	- Take VERSION_FROM from lib/File/Slurp/Remote.pm

0.46	Sat Oct 10 09:24:24 PM EDT 2026
	[ Bug Fixes ]
	- Fix module NAME field in Makefile.PL

0.45	Tue Sep 22 11:39:52 AM EDT 2026
	[ Bug Fixes ]
	- New release, new number 0.45 fixes RT#131984 since something was up with 0.44
	[ Enhancements ]
	- Use GitHub Actions

= 2026/09/22 - 0.43

New maintainer - nhorne@cpan.org
Fix packaging error: CanonicalHostnames wasn't in the MANIFEST.

= 2011/06/15 - 0.42

Add File::Slurp::Remote::CanonicalHostnames.  It is tested by
the regression suite in Proc::JobQueue.

= 2009/09/25 - 0.41

= 2009/08/03 - 0.4 

Allow ssh/scp commands to be overridden.

Add t/remote_slurp.t

Change File::Slurp::Remote::BrokenDNS so that it uses DNS when it can.
Setting $ENV{BROKEN_DNS_WORKAROUND} restores the old behavior.

Bugfixes for reading/writing local compressed files.

= 2009/07/23 - 0.3

Initial revision
